4. **`/home/box/git/github/somewm/objects/client.c:2179-2191`** — `client_geometry_refresh()` that triggers `apply_geometry_to_wlroots()`

5. **`/home/box/git/github/sway/sway/desktop/xwayland.c:267-279`** — Reference: Sway's correct approach (unconditional position update)

This is the root cause of Steam menus appearing at wrong positions — the compositor's internal scene graph knows the correct position, but never tells the X11 window system.

