- We call `_exit(1)` (not `exit(1)`) on `execvp` failure to avoid running `atexit` handlers on partially destroyed state
- The cleanup order matches `cleanup()` exactly, which has been tested and is known to work
- We skip `luaA_cleanup()` because we are inside a Lua call -- the OS frees memory via `execvp`

